WEBVTT

00:00:02.240 --> 00:00:03.930
We made it, huh?

00:00:03.930 --> 00:00:04.550
Yes.

00:00:04.550 --> 00:00:06.440
It's our long-awaited return

00:00:07.010 --> 00:00:08.330
to Osaka.

00:00:15.960 --> 00:00:17.770
<i>I've finally returned.</i>

00:00:20.550 --> 00:00:23.360
Osaka's always so full of life.

00:00:24.800 --> 00:00:26.880
Don't go too far, okay?

00:00:29.580 --> 00:00:30.740
Lord Keiji!

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:33.660
Long time no see!

00:00:33.660 --> 00:00:37.330
What a surprise! You guys been all right?

00:00:37.330 --> 00:00:39.760
Lord Keiji must know a lot of people.

00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:42.270
They all seem to be shady, though.

00:00:43.810 --> 00:00:45.990
<i>I see a lot of vagabond samurai.</i>

00:00:46.670 --> 00:00:49.230
<i>Then the Toyotomi clan really is...</i>

00:00:56.540 --> 00:00:58.530
You're the critter from back then!

00:01:03.800 --> 00:01:07.520
Sorry if my pet caused you any trouble!

00:01:09.010 --> 00:01:10.270
I knew it.

00:01:11.210 --> 00:01:13.260
Tsukimaru, you bad boy...

00:01:14.750 --> 00:01:16.720
It's been a while, Lady Kai.

00:01:17.180 --> 00:01:20.170
We've been expecting you, Lord Yukimura.

00:01:20.170 --> 00:01:22.970
And the walking fashion show over 
there must be Keiji Maeda, yes?

00:01:24.560 --> 00:01:27.100
Guess I'm more famous than I thought.

00:01:28.170 --> 00:01:30.260
Lord Hideyori's waiting.

00:01:30.260 --> 00:01:32.110
I'll take you to him.

00:03:09.600 --> 00:03:10.710
What a nice breeze.

00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:17.540
I brought them, Lord Hideyori.

00:03:18.060 --> 00:03:19.600
<i>So that's...</i>

00:03:24.470 --> 00:03:26.910
My father always used to say that 
Mitsunari was the brains,

00:03:26.910 --> 00:03:30.100
and Yukimura was the brawn.

00:03:30.500 --> 00:03:32.100
Lord Hideyoshi said that?

00:03:40.340 --> 00:03:42.110
You're more handsome than I expected.

00:03:45.030 --> 00:03:46.120
Keiji...

00:03:46.120 --> 00:03:48.180
Your uncle, Toshiie,

00:03:48.180 --> 00:03:50.620
took care of me a lot when I was younger.

00:03:52.570 --> 00:03:57.710
The arrival of famous warriors like yourselves 
should raise morale within the castle.

00:03:58.910 --> 00:04:00.840
Is war upon us?

00:04:02.360 --> 00:04:04.160
That's for the wind to decide.

00:04:10.080 --> 00:04:12.460
Soon, a mighty wind will blow from the east,

00:04:13.100 --> 00:04:15.950
in a bid to remove all obstacles from its path.

00:04:16.620 --> 00:04:20.900
However, I don't intend to 
let the wind have its way.

00:04:26.990 --> 00:04:30.160
I have to say I quite like that man.

00:04:30.160 --> 00:04:31.790
How about you?

00:04:32.040 --> 00:04:36.010
I believe he has a firm resolve.

00:04:36.010 --> 00:04:39.170
When you're traveling around the 
country, it really hits you.

00:04:39.170 --> 00:04:43.920
Even dogs by the wayside think the Tokugawa 
clan has the nation in its grasp.

00:04:44.240 --> 00:04:46.930
And despite all of that, 
Hideyori wants to stand up to them.

00:04:46.930 --> 00:04:49.430
He's a real daredevil.

00:04:49.800 --> 00:04:52.660
The apple doesn't fall far from the tree, huh?

00:04:52.660 --> 00:04:53.530
Indeed.

00:04:54.070 --> 00:04:57.280
My uncle was always Hideyoshi's right-hand man.

00:04:57.280 --> 00:04:58.930
Lord Toshiie Maeda?

00:04:58.930 --> 00:04:59.980
Yeah.

00:05:01.480 --> 00:05:05.970
Before, didn't you say that you 
would live for your beliefs?

00:05:06.430 --> 00:05:07.190
Yes.

00:05:07.530 --> 00:05:10.200
Then maybe I should follow in my uncle's footsteps

00:05:10.200 --> 00:05:13.880
and have one last party by Hideyori's side.

00:05:33.850 --> 00:05:35.330
<i>Lord Mitsunari,</i>

00:05:35.790 --> 00:05:39.640
<i>I have returned to Osaka.</i>

00:05:47.290 --> 00:05:48.990
Where are you headed, Lord Yukimura?

00:05:49.530 --> 00:05:51.020
To take a look around the castle.

00:05:51.020 --> 00:05:52.380
I'll accompany you.

00:05:54.330 --> 00:05:56.250
No, you should get some rest.

00:05:58.030 --> 00:06:00.800
It was a long journey from Kudoyama to here.

00:06:00.800 --> 00:06:01.980
You must be tired.

00:06:01.980 --> 00:06:04.380
Not at all. I want to accompany you.

00:06:04.380 --> 00:06:05.470
If you insist.

00:06:05.470 --> 00:06:07.510
Don't push yourself, though.

00:06:12.770 --> 00:06:14.750
<i>I'll follow you anywhere.</i>

00:06:14.750 --> 00:06:17.890
<i>I'm your ninja, after all.</i>

00:06:22.360 --> 00:06:26.030
Edo Castle

00:06:27.850 --> 00:06:29.000
So...

00:06:30.120 --> 00:06:34.050
What kind of man was Hideyori Toyotomi?

00:06:34.050 --> 00:06:37.170
Well, he was an enigma.

00:06:37.640 --> 00:06:39.580
What goes through his mind is a total mystery.

00:06:40.170 --> 00:06:43.370
But I couldn't help but be awed by him.

00:06:44.120 --> 00:06:48.300
I felt he was truly a man fit 
to lead the Toyotomi clan.

00:06:51.670 --> 00:06:53.920
I cannot wait for our meeting.

00:07:15.430 --> 00:07:17.700
Yukimura went to Osaka.

00:07:19.260 --> 00:07:22.380
I could not stop him.

00:07:23.190 --> 00:07:26.120
This time, we might have 
to prepare for the worst.

00:07:27.410 --> 00:07:30.180
There's no turning back, is there?

00:07:33.690 --> 00:07:38.220
All Yukimura and I can do is see how 
far the paths we've chosen take us.

00:07:40.020 --> 00:07:41.350
Lord Nobuyuki...

00:07:43.320 --> 00:07:45.510
No matter what happens,

00:07:46.020 --> 00:07:48.230
I shall help you shoulder your burden!

00:07:49.880 --> 00:07:50.740
Ina...

00:07:56.450 --> 00:07:59.290
A Few Days Later

00:08:02.850 --> 00:08:05.060
Be careful, and have a safe journey.

00:08:06.340 --> 00:08:08.360
Open the gates!

00:08:12.910 --> 00:08:14.180
Lord Kiyomasa...

00:08:14.180 --> 00:08:15.180
Lord Masanori!

00:08:20.270 --> 00:08:23.560
Please let us serve you!

00:08:23.940 --> 00:08:27.060
Please use our lives for the 
Toyotomi clan's betterment!

00:08:28.050 --> 00:08:30.070
It's too late for that!

00:08:30.720 --> 00:08:33.200
After siding with Ieyasu, how dare 
you ingrates say that?!

00:08:33.740 --> 00:08:36.200
We can't trust you!

00:08:37.680 --> 00:08:39.530
Get out of here!

00:08:39.530 --> 00:08:41.510
Yeah, leave!

00:08:42.970 --> 00:08:43.710
I'll allow it.

00:08:46.070 --> 00:08:48.040
Kiyomasa, Masanori,

00:08:48.040 --> 00:08:48.840
come with me.

00:08:49.260 --> 00:08:50.710
Yes, my lord!

00:08:59.140 --> 00:09:02.970
Hideyori Toyotomi made his way 
to Nijo Castle, in Kyoto,

00:09:03.780 --> 00:09:06.730
where he was to meet Ieyasu Tokugawa.

00:09:06.730 --> 00:09:10.230
Nijo Castle

00:09:13.120 --> 00:09:15.990
Lord Hideyori Toyotomi is here.

00:09:34.710 --> 00:09:36.420
What's the meaning of this?

00:09:38.370 --> 00:09:39.800
Is there a problem?

00:09:40.060 --> 00:09:43.810
Shouldn't the seat of honor be 
reserved for Lord Hideyori?

00:09:44.210 --> 00:09:46.710
You dare to look down on the Toyotomi clan?

00:09:55.900 --> 00:09:57.820
I'll be fine here.

00:10:03.250 --> 00:10:05.410
It's been too long.

00:10:10.140 --> 00:10:12.160
Thanks to your efforts,

00:10:12.160 --> 00:10:14.920
it looks like the country's finally calmed down.

00:10:15.250 --> 00:10:19.400
You did a fine job of carrying the 
torch my late father left behind.

00:10:19.400 --> 00:10:20.800
You humble me.

00:10:21.060 --> 00:10:24.580
But for a man trying to create a peaceful world,

00:10:25.030 --> 00:10:27.430
it sure seems as though you love warfare.

00:10:27.950 --> 00:10:30.120
Me? A warmonger?

00:10:30.550 --> 00:10:32.190
You could not be further from the truth.

00:10:32.550 --> 00:10:34.030
Really?

00:10:34.620 --> 00:10:37.120
With your powers,

00:10:37.120 --> 00:10:39.570
you should have been able to prevent 
the Battle of Sekigahara.

00:10:39.740 --> 00:10:44.810
I didn't want to take that step, but to protect 
the Toyotomi clan's world, I had to.

00:10:46.810 --> 00:10:47.830
If you say so.

00:10:48.250 --> 00:10:49.940
Speaking of warfare,

00:10:50.390 --> 00:10:55.000
I hear vagabond samurai from across the 
nation are gathering at Osaka Castle.

00:10:56.410 --> 00:11:00.450
Rumor says you're preparing for war 
against the Tokugawa clan.

00:11:01.130 --> 00:11:05.660
I'm only helping the samurai who 
lost their masters at Sekigahara.

00:11:06.230 --> 00:11:11.000
Ignore them, and the voices opposing the 
Tokugawa clan would only grow louder.

00:11:11.000 --> 00:11:13.460
You should actually be grateful to me.

00:11:13.460 --> 00:11:17.070
Is it true that Yukimura Sanada 
is now at Osaka Castle?

00:11:18.760 --> 00:11:21.280
Yes... Around thirty of them, I'd say.

00:11:22.400 --> 00:11:24.500
Yukimura is a famous man.

00:11:24.500 --> 00:11:29.540
There are plenty who wish to use his 
name to make a lot of money.

00:11:29.970 --> 00:11:33.150
And there's no way to tell which is the real one.

00:11:33.560 --> 00:11:34.750
Lord Hidetada,

00:11:34.750 --> 00:11:36.800
if you don't mind, could you 
come identify him for us?

00:11:39.320 --> 00:11:41.260
Regardless of how it happened,

00:11:41.260 --> 00:11:45.800
that rumor of your taking up arms 
is, in itself, a cause of unrest.

00:11:46.240 --> 00:11:48.240
In order to quell that rumor,

00:11:48.240 --> 00:11:51.310
I'd like you to leave Osaka Castle

00:11:51.670 --> 00:11:53.810
and move to Edo Castle.

00:11:58.500 --> 00:12:00.070
I won't go to Edo.

00:12:00.810 --> 00:12:02.000
I don't like the place.

00:12:02.000 --> 00:12:04.820
Besides, if I left, the women in Osaka 
Castle would be saddened.

00:12:05.110 --> 00:12:05.720
What are you—

00:12:05.720 --> 00:12:08.100
If you wish to live with me that badly,

00:12:08.450 --> 00:12:10.790
why not come to Osaka instead?

00:12:11.430 --> 00:12:14.510
You're a retired man, now that you've 
relinquished the post of shogun.

00:12:14.810 --> 00:12:17.040
Why don't we pass our days playing shogi?

00:12:20.580 --> 00:12:24.200
Unfortunately, I don't care much for Osaka myself.

00:12:24.200 --> 00:12:27.680
Furthermore, Hidetada is inexperienced.

00:12:28.550 --> 00:12:32.480
And the constructions around Edo 
Castle are yet to be completed.

00:12:32.900 --> 00:12:35.030
I hear Edo's prospering,

00:12:35.420 --> 00:12:38.480
and that the castle grows bigger by the day.

00:12:38.760 --> 00:12:42.240
It sounds almost like the Osaka 
Castle that my father built.

00:12:45.930 --> 00:12:49.060
Do you wish to make Edo the new political center?

00:12:49.540 --> 00:12:51.770
If so, you need only come out and say it...

00:12:54.250 --> 00:12:56.370
"Please give us the nation."

00:13:02.870 --> 00:13:05.260
If I do, will you hand it over?

00:13:13.540 --> 00:13:15.020
No, I won't.

00:13:24.940 --> 00:13:26.530
Who does that brat think he is?

00:13:26.830 --> 00:13:30.530
That mocking attitude of his was outrageous!

00:13:30.530 --> 00:13:31.790
Please calm down.

00:13:32.060 --> 00:13:33.100
Father,

00:13:33.100 --> 00:13:36.500
we have no choice but to force 
the Toyotomi clan to yield!

00:13:36.500 --> 00:13:38.300
Lord Hidetada, that's...

00:13:39.430 --> 00:13:40.290
You're right.

00:13:40.290 --> 00:13:41.870
Father...

00:13:41.870 --> 00:13:42.950
Takatora,

00:13:42.950 --> 00:13:45.880
send orders to feudal lords 
across the country at once!

00:13:46.110 --> 00:13:47.710
Right away, sir.

00:13:48.280 --> 00:13:50.250
Are you sure, my lord?

00:13:50.250 --> 00:13:52.060
Isn't this a bit premature—

00:13:52.060 --> 00:13:53.520
We cannot afford to wait!

00:13:54.260 --> 00:13:57.680
Nobuyuki, didn't you say before

00:13:57.680 --> 00:14:01.370
that Lord Hideyori was a man fit 
to lead the Toyotomi clan?

00:14:01.370 --> 00:14:02.190
Yes.

00:14:03.130 --> 00:14:05.000
Indeed he is.

00:14:05.000 --> 00:14:06.420
In fact, he's more than that.

00:14:06.420 --> 00:14:08.700
He could very well stand atop this entire nation.

00:14:10.030 --> 00:14:14.620
He has all the qualities of a leader, 
including the power to attract people.

00:14:14.620 --> 00:14:18.580
I see he has inherited Lord Hideyoshi's 
immense charisma.

00:14:19.250 --> 00:14:22.340
He is too dangerous to be left alone.

00:14:22.590 --> 00:14:25.500
That he would make you feel so threatened...

00:14:25.500 --> 00:14:27.840
Hideyori is a terrifying man.

00:14:28.080 --> 00:14:31.120
Even if Lord Hideyori himself 
doesn't want to go to war,

00:14:31.120 --> 00:14:33.680
people who once served the Toyotomi clan,

00:14:33.680 --> 00:14:38.270
and those who oppose the Tokugawa clan, 
will call him their rightful lord and master,

00:14:38.270 --> 00:14:40.960
and go to Osaka Castle.

00:14:41.390 --> 00:14:45.190
Apparently, tens of thousands of soldiers 
have already gathered at Osaka.

00:14:45.600 --> 00:14:47.910
Are you saying that if we don't do something,

00:14:47.910 --> 00:14:51.860
the country will be engulfed in war and, 
before long, return to chaos?

00:14:52.390 --> 00:14:54.490
That we have not a moment to lose?

00:14:54.770 --> 00:14:56.120
Exactly.

00:14:56.380 --> 00:14:59.980
The Tokugawa and Toyotomi clans, allies for 
so long, can stand together no more?

00:15:00.540 --> 00:15:05.630
Lord Hideyori should know that better than anyone.

00:15:08.630 --> 00:15:12.140
Yonezawa Castle

00:15:16.220 --> 00:15:19.390
So it has come to this. The Tokugawa 
want to wipe out the Toyotomi clan.

00:15:20.400 --> 00:15:21.520
<i>Yukimura...</i>

00:15:40.810 --> 00:15:41.650
Hey!

00:15:42.160 --> 00:15:42.670
What?

00:15:43.580 --> 00:15:44.750
Perfect timing.

00:15:45.220 --> 00:15:46.920
Care for a drink?

00:15:48.390 --> 00:15:49.670
Join us, Yukimura!

00:15:56.310 --> 00:15:59.560
A drink tastes best when shared with a group.

00:16:04.600 --> 00:16:07.000
Yukimura, we...

00:16:09.410 --> 00:16:11.690
We've been wanting to talk to you.

00:16:16.130 --> 00:16:18.830
You guys must've needed balls 
of steel to come back here.

00:16:19.140 --> 00:16:22.710
We never once considered ourselves 
as having left the Toyotomi clan!

00:16:24.510 --> 00:16:28.340
We all merely walked down 
the path we believed in.

00:16:28.740 --> 00:16:30.260
I understand.

00:16:30.260 --> 00:16:31.650
I really do,

00:16:31.650 --> 00:16:32.840
and so does Lord Mitsunari.

00:16:35.270 --> 00:16:36.470
Mitsunari...

00:16:42.810 --> 00:16:45.520
Sure is getting gloomy around here.

00:16:45.520 --> 00:16:47.480
Well, drink up!

00:16:55.420 --> 00:16:59.490
With this, we've swallowed 
all our regrets and tears.

00:16:59.490 --> 00:17:03.000
Why don't we share a cup to 
signify our alliance now?

00:17:11.740 --> 00:17:14.760
The Toyotomi clan received a 
letter from the Tokugawa.

00:17:15.070 --> 00:17:18.580
It offered them the choice to either 
have Hideyori move to Edo Castle

00:17:18.580 --> 00:17:22.680
or for the entire Toyotomi clan to leave 
Osaka and accept a change of domain,

00:17:22.680 --> 00:17:25.520
the cruelest of choices.

00:17:25.830 --> 00:17:27.060
They've gotta be kidding!

00:17:27.060 --> 00:17:29.020
Who in their right minds would accept that?

00:17:29.230 --> 00:17:29.800
That's right!

00:17:29.800 --> 00:17:31.520
We must reject it!

00:17:32.010 --> 00:17:35.380
If we refuse to comply with either one, 
the Tokugawa clan will attack Osaka.

00:17:35.380 --> 00:17:37.660
Bring it on, I say!

00:17:38.150 --> 00:17:42.050
Osaka Castle is the finest in all the land, 
built by Lord Hideyoshi himself.

00:17:42.050 --> 00:17:43.300
Its defenses are perfect.

00:17:43.300 --> 00:17:44.290
Lord Hideyori,

00:17:44.540 --> 00:17:47.410
we are all prepared for war!

00:17:49.550 --> 00:17:50.290
Yukimura...

00:17:50.570 --> 00:17:51.320
Yes, sir.

00:17:51.320 --> 00:17:52.840
What do you think?

00:17:53.150 --> 00:17:55.850
If it were me, I would attack from the south.

00:17:56.450 --> 00:18:00.300
I took a look around the castle 
from an attacker's perspective.

00:18:01.030 --> 00:18:07.060
Yes, Osaka Castle is surrounded 
by rivers on three sides,

00:18:07.060 --> 00:18:09.560
and it does have multiple lines of defense,

00:18:10.320 --> 00:18:12.790
making it hard to fell.

00:18:12.790 --> 00:18:15.320
However, if the outer wall were breached,

00:18:15.320 --> 00:18:17.110
the sheer size of the outermost enclosure

00:18:17.110 --> 00:18:19.780
makes it susceptible to being overrun 
by a large number of enemy troops.

00:18:20.500 --> 00:18:21.660
What?

00:18:22.310 --> 00:18:24.540
If I were to attack this castle,

00:18:24.900 --> 00:18:27.560
I would breach the wall on the southern 
side, where there's no moat,

00:18:27.560 --> 00:18:30.080
and then march to the opposite side in one fell swoop.

00:18:31.450 --> 00:18:33.890
This may be the finest castle in the country,

00:18:33.890 --> 00:18:36.460
but we don't stand a chance 
if they breach that wall.

00:18:37.540 --> 00:18:39.220
Then what should we do?

00:18:40.970 --> 00:18:42.410
Leave it to me.

00:19:00.050 --> 00:19:01.740
This is pretty large in scale.

00:19:02.000 --> 00:19:03.630
Is this what I think it is?

00:19:03.630 --> 00:19:04.650
Yes.

00:19:04.650 --> 00:19:06.260
I'm building a fortress.

00:19:06.260 --> 00:19:07.370
A detached bailey, huh?

00:19:07.640 --> 00:19:10.090
With this, we can hold off the enemy.

00:19:11.770 --> 00:19:14.380
I've never seen one so big.

00:19:14.620 --> 00:19:18.160
Guess we'll have to call it "Sanada Maru."

00:19:18.160 --> 00:19:20.010
The Sanada Maru, you say?

00:19:20.650 --> 00:19:23.600
A massive bailey that's on a par 
with the main keep's defenses.

00:19:23.600 --> 00:19:26.390
What else could we call it 
but the "Sanada Maru"?

00:19:26.700 --> 00:19:28.200
Sounds good to me!

00:19:28.200 --> 00:19:30.270
Yeah, it's the Sanada Maru.

00:19:30.600 --> 00:19:32.330
Did you hear that? They said, "Sanada Maru."

00:19:33.990 --> 00:19:37.780
Let's send the Tokugawa clan packing with this.

00:19:38.080 --> 00:19:40.150
We won't let anyone through!

00:19:40.630 --> 00:19:42.870
No matter how big an army attacks,

00:19:42.870 --> 00:19:44.910
let's defend Lord Hideyoshi's castle to the last.

00:19:45.150 --> 00:19:45.990
Yes!

00:19:46.910 --> 00:19:51.340
I can't wait for Sanada Maru to be complete.

00:19:57.620 --> 00:19:59.130
The Sanada Maru...

00:20:01.090 --> 00:20:04.930
Following Ieyasu's order to attack Osaka,

00:20:04.930 --> 00:20:07.800
feudal lords from all over the 
country headed into battle.

00:20:17.490 --> 00:20:22.420
Ieyasu himself departed Edo, 
massive army in tow.

00:20:26.580 --> 00:20:29.150
While marching toward Osaka,

00:20:29.150 --> 00:20:32.700
the Tokugawa army defeated the Toyotomi 
forces in various skirmishes.

00:20:34.850 --> 00:20:36.420
And finally,

00:20:36.420 --> 00:20:40.000
Tokugawa forces, approximately 200,000 strong,

00:20:40.000 --> 00:20:42.200
surrounded Osaka Castle.

00:20:42.860 --> 00:20:46.690
On the other hand, the Toyotomi army 
numbered fewer than 100,000.

00:20:47.230 --> 00:20:52.140
<i>The Toyotomi clan might be trying to see 
the continuation of Hideyoshi's dream.</i>

00:20:52.140 --> 00:20:55.730
<i>But unfortunately for them, they will 
never have that dream again.</i>

00:21:31.350 --> 00:21:34.060
Lord Hideyori can be pretty classy, huh?

00:21:34.770 --> 00:21:37.060
The colors of the armor he gave us

00:21:37.340 --> 00:21:40.310
make me feel like I'm back at Ueda Castle.

00:21:41.490 --> 00:21:42.600
In the past,

00:21:42.600 --> 00:21:46.700
the Sanada clan soldiers fought 
bravely in the face of death.

00:21:47.280 --> 00:21:49.160
And on this day, in Osaka Castle,

00:21:49.160 --> 00:21:52.600
their spirit revives along with Yukimura.

00:21:57.320 --> 00:21:58.410
<i>Yukimura...</i>

00:22:04.880 --> 00:22:09.890
<i>Episode 9</i>

00:22:04.880 --> 00:22:09.890
<i>The Osaka Tempest</i>

00:23:41.890 --> 00:23:45.150
Sengoku Musou 
High School

00:23:41.890 --> 00:23:45.150
9th Period

00:23:45.710 --> 00:23:48.380
I made lunch, Lord Nobuyuki.

00:23:48.380 --> 00:23:50.010
Thanks as always, Ina.

00:23:50.010 --> 00:23:51.760
Feel free to dig in, Yukimura, Kunoichi.

00:23:51.760 --> 00:23:52.610
Thank you very much.

00:23:52.610 --> 00:23:53.780
Wow!

00:23:53.780 --> 00:23:55.760
Amazing!

00:23:56.280 --> 00:23:58.740
Guys with girlfriends sure have it good.

00:23:58.740 --> 00:24:01.140
Now, dig in!

00:24:04.040 --> 00:24:06.930
I packed it to the brim with healthy stuff!

00:24:06.930 --> 00:24:08.840
That actually looks unhealthy instead.

00:24:08.840 --> 00:24:09.880
<i>To Be Continued</i>

00:24:09.880 --> 00:24:24.800
<i>Next Episode</i>

00:24:10.510 --> 00:24:13.430
The next battle is the Siege 
of Osaka's first chapter.

00:24:13.800 --> 00:24:17.100
It won't give an inch, even if the 
Earth crumbles around it.

00:24:17.290 --> 00:24:19.560
Capable of defending against thousands of soldiers,

00:24:19.560 --> 00:24:21.770
its name is the Sanada Maru.

00:24:21.980 --> 00:24:24.500
Next time: "Fortress Beyond Compare."

00:24:22.850 --> 00:24:24.800
<i>Episode Ten 
Fortress Beyond 
Compare</i>
